# Jenova — .gitignore
#
# Consolidated 2026-09-01 (Session 019). Rules for paths that no longer exist
# were removed rather than carried: /jenova-cli, /cli-agent, /models, /backups,
# conductor/, /.kdev4, the installation-audit artifacts and the shellcheck
# report. Duplicate entries for .jenova/ and .crush/ were folded into one.
#
# ONE KNOWN INCONSISTENCY, deliberately left for the USER to decide:
# `bin/jenova` is listed below AND is tracked in git, because it was committed
# before the rule existed and .gitignore does not untrack an existing file. It
# is therefore a ~2 MB binary re-committed on every build. Untracking it
# (`git rm --cached bin/jenova`) removes it from the repository on the next
# commit, which changes what a clone gets — so it is not done here.

# --- Build artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
# Both binaries are built by `nimble core` and `nimble gui` (never `make` — this
# project has no Makefile, D-AM).
/bin/jenova
/bin/jenova-core
/bin/llama-server
/public/
/external/ext_bin/
nimcache/

*.o
*.so
*.a
*.dylib

# --- jvim: TRACKED ON PURPOSE — do not add an ignore rule here ---------------
# `jvim/` is the configuration for the Neovim this application embeds, added by
# the USER 2026-09-01 and ruled **D-BS**: it is configuration, not product Lua,
# so the no-Lua rule (D-AM, D-AZ) does not archive it and it is not ignored.
#
# `jvim/pack/` is vendored third-party plugins and is tracked deliberately —
# the distribution's promise is zero package manager and no network on first
# boot, which only holds if the vendored tree ships with it. ~28 MB total.
#
# Its runtime noise (shada, swap, undo, *.log) is handled by `jvim/.gitignore`,
# which git honours in place. `*.log` below also covers `jvim/nvim.log`.

# --- Models (never commit multi-GB weights) ----------------------------------
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.h5
*.tflite
*.bin

# --- Runtime data and private state ------------------------------------------
/var/log/**
/var/cache/**
!/var/log/.gitkeep
!/var/cache/.gitkeep
/var/state/
/.system/

# --- AI assistant working directories ----------------------------------------
# `.devdocs/` is deliberately NOT here: the process record is tracked and public
# in repository history. A previous revision of this file claimed otherwise and
# was wrong on both counts.
.claude/
.crush/
.gemini/
.jenova/
.cursor/
.copilot/
.codeium/
.aider/
.continue/
.tabnine/
.windsurf/

# --- Environment, keys and secrets -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.csr
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*.secret
*_secret*
*.token
credentials.json
secrets.json
auth.json

# --- Local configuration overrides -------------------------------------------
# `jenova.local.conf` is the USER's machine file. `hardware.applyProfile`
# never writes it, and that is asserted (D-BN) — silently overwriting it is the
# one way the profile feature could do real damage.
/etc/jenova.conf.local
/etc/jenova.conf.bak.*
/etc/jenova.local.conf

# --- Databases and session data ----------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.jsonl
.bash_history
.zsh_history
.history

# --- Logs, archives and crash dumps ------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.7z
*.bak
*.tmp
core
core.*
*.dmp

# --- System and IDE ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*~
*.swp
*.swo
\#*\#

# --- Web UI build output (jca_web is frozen, D-Z — read it, never edit it) ----
/jca_web/node_modules/
/jca_web/.svelte-kit/
/jca_web/build/
/jca_web/src-tauri/target/
